  "notes": [
    "Inputs: confirm split only (5600 HOGs = split.tsv; pair tables, branch tables, E6 triplets all split=='confirm'); primary pairs 866959 = sum C(|S_h|,2) for every confirm HOG in all 3 alignments; no duplicate pair_ids; 29117 confirm E6 triplets (+7383 tune = 36500 = hogs_e6.tsv).",
    "E1/E2 n_excluded bookkeeping: the 'hog_lt_min_pairs_or_range' bucket also counts weight-0 pairs already counted in 'pair_weight0_fail_or_sat' (E1: 20891 vs 20837 own; E2: 20932 vs 20877), so buckets + n_units exceed the primary-pair count by 54/55. n_units (pairs entering the fit) is correct. Reporting only.",
    "fail_frac per HOG recomputed from the pair table (not ok, or AA/metric saturated) matches hogs_endpoint_cols exactly; same 183 (tdi) / 140 (lddt) excluded HOGs.",
    "D31 wording vs implementation: DEVIATIONS says the PB pseudo-data use 'edge-level, tree-additive noise'; the code uses a tree-additive DESIGN (x_hat = X b_AA) with independent pair-level Sigma_ij noise. The independent PB here follows the implemented reading and reproduces pb_bias within MC error (E1 z=0.67, E2 z=1.06). Documentation fix suggested.",
    "2 HOGs (HOG0022006, HOG0102266) have NaN misfit_ratio and are kept in E3-E5 (NaN is not > tau). Consistent with the rule as written; worth a line in the report.",
    "E5 n_contrasts=146 counts contrasts with finite x_v; one of them has non-finite y_v (sum of 3Di path lengths <= 0 on one side) so beta uses 145. Reporting nuance.",
    "E5 floor F (P=100 parametric bootstrap needing per-HOG WLS operators) was not re-simulated; sigma2_L checked as sigma2_obs - F. beta_contrast depends on random c_v/vx_v (200 HOG-pigeonhole reps); own 5 seeds give 0.583 +- 0.008 vs project 0.572 (1.4 sd).",
    "E6a uses the plan's seeded P1 choice (stage e6_p1_choice) -> exact match; orientation-averaged E6a = 0.03075 (sign and conclusion unchanged).",
    "Branch tables (b, b_se, cov_aa, ages) were used as inputs and not re-derived from pairs; their tip correction (b = b_raw - eta/2 on terminal 3Di edges) and tau = midpoint were checked."
  ],
